cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Lignin Nanoparticle Lab: a population-balance model of lignin nanoparticle formation and breakup"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adesanya
    given-names: Taiwo Zacchaeus
    affiliation: "University of Illinois Chicago"
abstract: >-
  Interactive browser model of lignin nanoparticle (LNP) formation by antisolvent
  addition, dilute-H2SO4 acid precipitation and sonication. Sectional population balance
  (nucleation, diffusion-limited growth, DLVO aggregation, stress-based breakage,
  engulfment micromixing) with DLS-comparable Z-average and PDI outputs.
keywords:
  - lignin nanoparticles
  - population balance
  - antisolvent precipitation
  - COSMO-RS
  - protic ionic liquids
  - DLS
